    <section class="prose prose-invert max-w-none space-y-8">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">1. The Fukuoka Advantage: Japan's National Strategic Special Zone</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          While Tokyo commands international headlines, Fukuoka City (located on the northern coast of Kyushu) has quietly built Japan's most aggressive startup support infrastructure. Designated as a National Strategic Special Zone for Global Startups and Job Creation by the Japanese Cabinet Office, Fukuoka operates under regulatory carve-outs designed specifically to bypass the bureaucratic gridlocks typical of Japanese corporate incorporation.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          For software engineers, solo founders, and digital creators, Fukuoka combines hyper-modern telecommunications with a compact, bicycle-friendly urban layout. The city's international airport (FUK) sits exactly 10 minutes by subway from the central Tenjin business district, offering direct 1.5-hour flights to Seoul, Shanghai, and Taipei, and 2-hour flights to Tokyo Haneda.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">2. Fukuoka Startup Visa Requirements and Step-by-Step Application</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          The standard Japanese "Business Manager" visa imposes strict pre-requisites: applicants must lease a physical, standalone commercial office and invest at least 5,000,000 JPY (~$34,000 USD) in paid-in capital or employ two full-time Japanese permanent residents before even submitting an application. The Fukuoka Startup Visa eliminates this chicken-and-egg problem by granting a designated "Designated Activities" status for 6 months to fulfill these milestones while living legally in Fukuoka.
        </p>
        
        <!-- Comparison Table -->
        <div class="overflow-x-auto my-6">
          <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse border border-slate-700 text-sm">
            <thead>
              <tr class="bg-slate-950 text-slate-200">
