          One of Fukuoka's strongest value propositions is the runway extension it affords bootstrapped software founders. In Tokyo (Minato, Shibuya, or Shinjuku), a modern 1LDK apartment costs between ¥180,000 and ¥280,000 per month ($1,200–$1,900 USD), plus substantial upfront non-refundable key money (*reikin*) and guarantor fees. In Fukuoka, comparable living quarters in Chuo-ku cost less than half.
        </p>

